<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE starlink-15-18 ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 Starlink Group 15-18 (SLC-4E) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Loft: FALCON 9 FAMILY SURROGATE, not this flight: altitude &amp; downrange vs time from SpaceX webcast telemetry of Iridium NEXT-7
(F9 Block 5, VSFB SLC-4E, 25 Jul 2018, ~9.6 t to 86.6 deg, droneship landing, MECO 146 s = 15-18 MECO T+2:26), 9 s running mean; range = integral of horizontal speed x R/(R+h).
Telemetry source: https://github.com/shahar603/Telemetry-Data/tree/master/Iridium%20NEXT%207 (analysed.json; data end T+508 s at 182.5 km). T+508-519 s EXTRAPOLATED (altitude held) to SECO-1 T+8:39.
Events (SpaceX sl-15-18 timeline https://www.spacex.com/launches/sl-15-18): Max-Q 1:08, MECO 2:26, sep 2:29, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:58, SECO-1 8:39;
then SES-2 53:07, SECO-2 53:08, deploy 1:01:59 (not in file). 27 Starlink V2 Mini Optimized, booster 18th flight (SpaceX; LL2 B1093) -&gt; OCISLY.
Azimuth basis: NAVAREA XII 747/26 (USCG LNM 56848) Hazard Area A, bearing pad -&gt; far-edge midpoint 29.692N -117.925E = 154.56 deg;
https://space-notices.com/notice/nav-warning-NAVAREA%20XII%20747%2F26 (alternate window 300402Z-300827Z OCT); i=70.004 deg (SpaceX vector, CelesTrak SupGP starlink-g15-18) formula gives 155.44 deg (consistent).
Velocity = d/dt of interpolated altitude and ground range (Earth-relative). Differences vs this flight: heavier payload (~15.5 t), lower parking orbit (SECO-1 orbit ~177 x 266 km derived).
T0: LL2 NET 2026-10-30T04:02:00Z (Thu 29 Oct 9:02 pm PDT), status Go; Spaceflight Now agrees (window opens 9:02 pm PDT).
Pad (LL2): 34.632000N -120.611000E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=154.56 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-10-30T04:02:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
